CRM → OLYMPUS API – CLOUD MIGRATION ASSESSMENT / OPEN QUESTIONS

Current State:
- CRM → Olympus application is currently running on VM/server infrastructure.
- CRM applications call the CRM → Olympus APIs through WIP/VIP/Apigee.
- The application receives CRM protobuf/binary payloads and publishes the data to Kafka.
- Current supported flows include:
  • Client Meeting
  • Client Action Item
  • Call Report
  • Productivity Metrics
- The application currently connects to Kafka using configured bootstrap servers, credentials and certificates.
- Start/stop activities are currently handled through server scripts / AutoSys jobs.
- Certificates and application configuration are currently maintained for the server-based deployment.

Cloud Migration Questions / Requirements:

1. API Hosting / Runtime
- Where will the CRM → Olympus API application run in the cloud?
- Will it be hosted on ECS/EKS/GKE or another Nucleus-supported runtime?
- What changes are required when moving the existing VM-based application to the cloud/container platform?
- How will DEV/UAT/PROD environments be maintained in the cloud?

2. API Authentication & Security
- How will authentication and authorization be handled for cloud-hosted CRM → Olympus APIs?
- Will consumers continue using OAuth/client ID/client secret through Apigee?
- Will the current Apigee layer remain or will there be a new cloud API gateway?
- Will existing consumer entitlements need to be recreated or migrated?
- How will application secrets/passwords be stored in the cloud?

3. Certificates / HTTPS
- How will certificates be managed for the cloud-hosted APIs?
- Today certificates are handled at server/WIP/VIP/application level.
- Will TLS termination be handled by cloud load balancer/API gateway instead of application code?
- Do existing VIP/WIP certificates need to be recreated or replaced?
- What is the certificate renewal/rotation process in cloud?

4. Kafka / Messaging
- What Kafka platform will CRM → Olympus use in the cloud?
- Are we moving to Confluent Kafka or another managed Kafka service?
- Will the existing Kafka bootstrap servers/topics change?
- How will Kafka authentication be handled in cloud?
- Will certificates/passwords currently used for Kafka connectivity change?

5. On-Prem Kafka vs Cloud Kafka
- If some CRM data remains on-prem and some moves to cloud, how will both Kafka environments be managed?
- Will CRM → Olympus need connectivity to both on-prem Kafka and cloud Kafka?
- Will there be separate topics for cloud-eligible and on-prem-only data?
- Who will perform routing between on-prem and cloud Kafka?

6. Cross-Border / CDBC Data Restrictions
- Some country/region data may not be approved for public cloud.
- How will CRM → Olympus determine which data can be published to cloud Kafka and which data must remain on-prem?
- Is CDBC/cross-border approval required for the CRM data currently being processed?
- Will routing rules be provided centrally or must CRM → Olympus implement them?

7. Protobuf Payload
- CRM → Olympus currently receives/publishes data in protobuf/binary format.
- Will protobuf continue to be supported in the cloud?
- Will the existing .proto schemas remain unchanged?
- Is Schema Registry required in the target Kafka platform?
- Will consumers need any payload/schema changes after migration?

8. Active-Active / Resiliency
- How will the current active-active processing model be maintained in cloud?
- Will AWS/GCP provide active-active automatically or does the application need to handle routing/failover?
- Will the application continue to send to primary/secondary environments?
- What will be the failover and disaster-recovery mechanism?

9. Network Connectivity
- How will cloud CRM → Olympus connect to systems that remain on-prem?
- Will PrivateLink/private connectivity/gateway be provided?
- What firewall/whitelisting changes will be required?
- Will WIP/VIP remain required or be replaced with cloud load-balancing services?
- Are any new ports/DNS entries required?

10. AutoSys / Scheduling / Start-Stop Jobs
- Today server/application start-stop activities are controlled through scripts/AutoSys.
- What is the equivalent mechanism in cloud?
- Will AutoSys continue to trigger cloud workloads?
- Should this be replaced by Databricks Scheduler, Databricks Workflows, Airflow, Kubernetes CronJob or platform-native scheduling?
- Will application start/stop even be required for containerized deployment?

11. Application Configuration
- How will current application.properties/environment-specific configurations be managed?
- Where will Kafka URLs, API URLs, client IDs, secrets and certificates be stored?
- Will configuration be managed using cloud secrets/config maps/vault?

12. Monitoring / Logging
- What replaces the existing server-based application logs?
- What centralized cloud logging/monitoring platform will be used?
- How will API failures, Kafka publish failures and application health be monitored?
- What alerting mechanism will be available?

13. Deployment / CI-CD
- How will the existing build/deployment pipeline change for cloud deployment?
- Will Jenkins remain or move to Harness/cloud-native deployment?
- What container/image repository will be used?
- What changes are required to the existing deployment scripts?

14. Consumer Impact
- Existing consumers include:
  • GSG CRM
  • TTS CRM
  • CCB CRM
  • Markets CRM
  • FX CRM
  • BCMA CRM
- Will consumers continue using the same Apigee URLs?
- If endpoints change, what migration/communication is required?
- Will existing client IDs/secrets continue to work?

15. Data Persistence / Database
- CRM → Olympus currently acts primarily as a pass-through application and does not maintain core business data locally.
- Confirm whether any application/audit/configuration persistence needs to move to a cloud database.
- If a database becomes necessary, should PostgreSQL/Lakebase be used instead of Oracle?

16. Migration Validation
- Perform end-to-end validation:
  CRM Consumer
      → Apigee/API Gateway
      → CRM → Olympus API
      → Protobuf processing
      → Kafka publish
      → Olympus downstream processing
- Validate both cloud-enabled and on-prem-restricted data scenarios.
- Validate failover/active-active behavior.
- Validate authentication, certificates, connectivity and monitoring.

Key Architecture Decisions Required:
- Target runtime/platform for CRM → Olympus
- API Gateway/Apigee strategy
- Kafka/Confluent strategy
- On-prem ↔ cloud connectivity model
- CDBC/cross-border data handling
- Certificate and secrets management
- Active-active/failover design
- Scheduling/AutoSys replacement
- Monitoring/logging solution
- CI/CD and deployment model




















