18. Correct Command – Convert PFX Directly to JKS
======================================================================

This is now the recommended approach.

Git Bash / Linux:

keytool -importkeystore \
-srckeystore CertAndKey.pfx \
-srcstoretype PKCS12 \
-destkeystore cacerts.jks \
-deststoretype JKS

Windows CMD one-line version:

keytool -importkeystore -srckeystore CertAndKey.pfx -srcstoretype PKCS12 -destkeystore cacerts.jks -deststoretype JKS

The command will prompt for:

Destination keystore password

Source keystore password

After successful conversion:

cacerts.jks

is created.

[ADD PFX TO JKS COMMAND SCREENSHOT HERE]

======================================================================
19. Why This Command Is Better
======================================================================

The PFX already contains:

Certificate + Private Key

keytool -importkeystore transfers the PrivateKeyEntry into the JKS.

Therefore we do not need to:

1. Download another generic JKS.
2. Generate a separate application private key.
3. Manually combine unrelated keystores.

Correct flow:

CMP-approved PFX
       ↓
keytool -importkeystore
       ↓
Application JKS

This is simpler and cleaner.

