32. Certificate Issue vs HTTP Issue
======================================================================

During troubleshooting, do not assume every API error is certificate-related.

SSL issue examples:

SSLHandshakeException

PKIX error

certificate_unknown

hostname verification error

These indicate certificate/TLS investigation.

HTTP 400:

400 Bad Request

TLS already succeeded.

Investigate:

payload

headers

request format

HTTP 404:

404 Not Found

TLS already succeeded.

Investigate:

URL

path

routing

Apigee/VIP/WIP mapping

HTTP 405:

405 Method Not Allowed

We saw this when opening a POST-only endpoint directly in Chrome.

Chrome sends GET when opening a URL.

The endpoint required POST.

Therefore 405 did not indicate a certificate problem.

